  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is no evidence for any design choice. The most critical uncertainty is the absolute performance floor: how well does the simplest possible configuration (RNA-only, single-profile, PCA-2000) perform? Establishing this baseline is essential before interpreting whether more complex encoders (scvi, scgpt), multiprofile aggregation (avgpool, transformer), image modalities, or multimodal fusion actually add value. Config_001 is the minimal configuration in the design space—no image encoder, no aggregation, no fusion—making it the cleanest reference point. All subsequent experiments can be understood as adding one or more design choices on top of this floor, which allows us to isolate the marginal contribution of each decision. Under a limited budget, spending one experiment on the simplest baseline maximizes the information gained per experiment by anchoring the entire comparison grid."
}

